I am getting the following error: Error saving rules - Line 1: mismatched input 'code' expecting {'function', 'import', 'service', 'rules_version'}

Can you provide new rules for firebase that I can paste in there?

It looks like you accidentally copied the **Markdown formatting words** (`code`, `2`, `JavaScript`) along with the actual rules. Firebase treats those words as invalid code, causing the syntax error.

Here are the clean rules. **Copy and paste exactly this block** into your Firebase Storage Rules tab:

```javascript
rules_version = '2';
service firebase.storage {
  match /b/{bucket}/o {
    match /{allPaths=**} {
      // Allow public read access (essential for downloading files and viewing images)
      allow read: if true;

      // Only allow authenticated admins to upload/delete
      allow write: if request.auth != null;
    }
  }
}
```

I have also updated the `storage.rules` file in your project to match this clean version, ensuring your local codebase is correct for future deployments.

To embed your Financial Resource Library into a WordPress site (including block themes like **Twenty Twenty-Five**), use the following script. 

This script is optimized to listen for the height updates your app already sends, ensuring there are no internal scrollbars and the library feels like a native part of your page.

### How to use:
1. Open your WordPress page editor.
2. Add a **Custom HTML** block where you want the library to appear.
3. Paste the code below into that block.
4. **Important:** Replace `'YOUR_APP_URL_HERE'` with the actual URL where your app is hosted (e.g., `https://your-project.web.app`).

```html
<div id="financial-library-container" style="width: 100%; overflow: hidden;">
    <div id="financial-library-loading" style="text-align: center; padding: 40px; color: #33424e; font-family: sans-serif;">
        <p>Loading Resource Library...</p>
    </div>
</div>

<script>
(function() {
    // 1. CONFIGURATION: Replace this with your actual hosted app URL
    var appUrl = 'YOUR_APP_URL_HERE'; 

    var container = document.getElementById('financial-library-container');
    var loader = document.getElementById('financial-library-loading');

    if (!container || appUrl === 'YOUR_APP_URL_HERE') {
        console.error('Financial Library Embed: Please provide a valid appUrl.');
        return;
    }

    // 2. CREATE THE IFRAME
    var iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
    iframe.src = appUrl;
    iframe.style.width = '100%';
    iframe.style.height = '600px'; // Initial starting height
    iframe.style.border = 'none';
    iframe.style.overflow = 'hidden';
    iframe.scrolling = 'no';
    iframe.title = 'Financial Resource Library';
    iframe.setAttribute('frameborder', '0');
    iframe.setAttribute('allowfullscreen', 'true');

    // 3. LISTEN FOR RESIZE MESSAGES
    window.addEventListener('message', function(event) {
        // Security Check: Verify the message comes from your app's domain
        try {
            var appOrigin = new URL(appUrl).origin;
            if (event.origin !== appOrigin) return;
        } catch (e) { return; }

        // Handle the specific resize event your app sends
        if (event.data && event.data.type === 'financial-library-resize' && typeof event.data.height === 'number') {
            // Add a small buffer (20px) to prevent micro-scrollbars in some browsers
            iframe.style.height = (event.data.height + 20) + 'px';

            // Hide loader once we get the first height update
            if (loader) {
                loader.style.display = 'none';
            }
        }
    }, false);

    // 4. MOUNT
    container.appendChild(iframe);
})();
</script>

<style>
    /* Prevent layout shift in Twenty Twenty-Five theme */
    #financial-library-container {
        margin-top: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        clear: both;
    }

    /* Ensure the iframe doesn't show a border on focus */
    iframe:focus {
        outline: none;
    }
</style>
```

### Key features of this script:
*   **Zero-Scrollbar Logic:** It uses the `ResizeObserver` data sent from your `index.tsx` to set the `iframe.style.height` in real-time.
*   **Theme Compatibility:** Twenty Twenty-Five uses a "Content Width" that can sometimes constrain blocks. This script uses `width: 100%` to ensure it fills whatever column or group block you place it in.
*   **Loading State:** Includes a simple "Loading..." message that disappears as soon as the app communicates its height, providing a better user experience.
*   **Smooth Integration:** Disables the iframe border and internal scrolling so the background of the app merges seamlessly with your WordPress site background.

Here is the updated embed script, pre-configured with your URL and optimized for the **Twenty Twenty-Five** theme. 

Copy and paste this entire block into a **Custom HTML** block in your WordPress editor:

```html
<div id="bp-money-library-root" style="width: 100%; position: relative; margin: 0 auto; clear: both;">
    <!-- Minimalist Loader -->
    <div id="bp-library-loader" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 60px 20px; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #33424e;">
        <div style="width: 40px; height: 40px; border: 3px solid #f3f3f3; border-top: 3px solid #3387ae; border-radius: 50%; animation: spin 1s linear infinite; margin-bottom: 15px;"></div>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500;">Loading Resource Library...</p>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    @keyframes spin {
        0% { transform: rotate(0deg); }
        100% { transform: rotate(360deg); }
    }

    /* Ensure no weird spacing in Twenty Twenty-Five block containers */
    .wp-block-custom-html {
        width: 100% !important;
    }

    #bp-money-library-root iframe {
        opacity: 0;
        transition: opacity 0.3s ease-in-out;
    }

    #bp-money-library-root iframe.loaded {
        opacity: 1;
    }
</style>

<script>
(function() {
    var APP_URL = 'https://financialresourcelibraryv3-fmhm.vercel.app/';
    var container = document.getElementById('bp-money-library-root');
    var loader = document.getElementById('bp-library-loader');

    if (!container) return;

    // Create the iframe
    var iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
    iframe.src = APP_URL;
    iframe.style.width = '100%';
    iframe.style.height = '600px'; // Initial fallback height
    iframe.style.border = 'none';
    iframe.style.display = 'block';
    iframe.style.overflow = 'hidden';
    iframe.setAttribute('scrolling', 'no');
    iframe.setAttribute('frameborder', '0');
    iframe.setAttribute('allowfullscreen', 'true');
    iframe.title = 'Financial Resource Library';

    // Append to container
    container.appendChild(iframe);

    // Listen for resize messages from the app
    window.addEventListener('message', function(event) {
        // Security check
        var origin = '';
        try {
            origin = new URL(APP_URL).origin;
        } catch(e) { return; }

        if (event.origin !== origin) return;

        // Handle height update
        if (event.data && event.data.type === 'financial-library-resize' && typeof event.data.height === 'number') {
            var newHeight = event.data.height;

            // Apply new height
            iframe.style.height = newHeight + 'px';

            // Visual polish: Reveal iframe and hide loader on first valid height message
            if (loader && loader.parentNode) {
                loader.style.display = 'none';
                iframe.classList.add('loaded');
            }
        }

        // Optional: Handle scrolls. If the app tells us to scroll up (e.g. after navigating),
        // we can scroll the WordPress window to the top of the container.
        if (event.data && event.data.type === 'financial-library-scroll-top') {
            container.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' });
        }
    }, false);
})();
</script>
```

### Why this works perfectly for your setup:
1.  **Twenty Twenty-Five Optimization:** The script uses `clear: both` and `width: 100%` to ensure it breaks out of any float issues or narrow column constraints common in modern WordPress block themes.
2.  **Smooth Entrance:** I added a CSS transition. Instead of the app "popping" in, it fades in elegantly once it communicates its initial height.
3.  **Automatic Resizing:** It listens specifically for the `financial-library-resize` event sent by your `App.tsx` file, ensuring that whether you are on the resource grid or the long Admin dashboard, the page height adjusts instantly.
4.  **No Scrollbars:** By setting `scrolling="no"` on the iframe and letting the parent handle the height, users will never see double scrollbars.

